/-! For a perfectoid Tate pair and a finite rational covering of a rational `U`, the augmented
alternating Čech complex of `O⁺` is almost exact (killed by every `ϖ^{1/pⁿ}`), exact at its first
two terms, termwise almost equal to that of `V ↦ O_X(V)°`, and so `H^i(U, O_X⁺)` is almost zero
for `i > 0` (Berkeley proof of Theorem 7.4.4; Sch12 proof of Proposition 6.14; KL II Corollary
3.3.20(c)). The termwise comparison `O_X(V)°/O_X⁺(V)` almost zero is
`PerfectoidSpace.rationalPairFunctor.isAlmostZero_powerBounded_quot_plus_affinoid`. -/

