--   Layer 5). It is affinoid perfectoid, presented by the zero ring with the zero plus ring.
--   [degenerate test]
-- IsAffinoidPerfectoid.spa_ecd34iv: not stated here; needs `Spa` as an adic space (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). For `R = ℤ_p^cycl[[T^{1/p^∞}]]⟨(p/T)^{1/p^∞}⟩[1/T]` (ECD Example
--   3.4(iv)), over no perfectoid field, `Spa(R, R°)` is affinoid perfectoid. [computation test]
-- spaHomEquiv_perfectoidField: not stated here; needs morphisms of adic spaces (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). For a perfectoid field `K`, morphisms `Spa(S, S⁺) → Spa(K, K°)` are the
