--   `Spa L ×_{Spa K} Spa L` strictly contains the image of `L° ⊗_{K°} L°`. [non-example test]
-- pullback_isPullback_adicSpace: not stated here; needs `IsPullback` in `AdicSpace` (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). The square is a pullback of adic spaces, and on affinoid pieces
--   `Spa(B ⊗̂ᵘ_A C) → Spa(B ⊗̂_A C)` is an isomorphism. [compatibility test]
-- pullback_tilt: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.tilt` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-spaces-and-glued-tilting). The fibre product of
--   `Y♭ → X♭ ← Z♭` in `Perf` is `(Y ×_X Z)♭`. [characterisation test]

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P2/tilting-commutes-with-fibre-products (lemma) -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackTiltIso: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.tilt` and
--   `PerfectoidSpace.pullback` (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-spaces-and-glued-tilting,
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). `(Y ×_X Z)♭ ≅ Y♭ ×_{X♭} Z♭` over the tilted projections; on affinoid
--   pieces it is `Perfectoid.completedTensorTiltIso` (with
--   `Perfectoid.completedTensorTiltIso_spec`).

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P2/fibre-products-over-analytic-base (construction) -/

/-! Over an analytic adic space `S`, `Y ×_S Z` exists in `Perfd`, glued from
`Spa(O_Y(U) ⊗̂ᵘ_A O_Z(V))` over affinoids `Spa(A, A⁺) ⊆ S` with `A` Tate; it is a fibre product
only for perfectoid test objects when `S` is not perfectoid. -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace` and analytic adic
--   spaces (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space, AdicSpaces Layer 5). The perfectoid
--   space `Y ×_S Z` for `S` analytic.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.fst: not stated here; needs
--   `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic` (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). The projection to `Y`;
--   likewise `.snd`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.condition: not stated here; needs morphisms of adic spaces
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). `fst ≫ f = snd ≫ g`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.lift: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). The unique `T → Y ×_S Z` for a perfectoid space `T`;
--   affinoid pair-level core: `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalyticSpaIso_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalyticSpaIso: not stated here; needs `Spa` in `AdicSpace`
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). Over affinoid pieces, `Spa B ×_{Spa A} Spa C ≅ Spa(B ⊗̂ᵘ_A C)`
--   in `Perfd`; pair-level core: `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalyticSpaIso_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalyticIsoPullback: not stated here; needs
--   `PerfectoidSpace.pullback` (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/fibre-products-of-perfectoid-spaces).
--   For `S` perfectoid the canonical map to `pullback f g` is an isomorphism; ring-level core:
--   `Perfectoid.isIso_toUniformization_completedTensor`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.isAffinoidPerfectoid: not stated here; needs
--   `PerfectoidSpace.IsAffinoidPerfectoid` (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). Ring-level core:
--   `Perfectoid.isPerfectoidTateRing_uniformCompletedTensor`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalyticRestrictIso: not stated here; needs open subspaces
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). `p⁻¹(U) ∩ q⁻¹(V) ≅ U ×_{S'} V`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.diagonalOverAnalytic: not stated here; needs
--   `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic` (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). The diagonal
--   `Y → Y ×_S Y`, used for analytic separatedness (PerfectoidSpaces:P8).
-- PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.surjective_points: not stated here; needs the underlying
--   spaces of adic spaces (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). `|Y ×_S Z| → |Y| ×_{|S|} |Z|` is
--   surjective; affinoid core: `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic.surjective_points_affinoid`.

namespace PerfectoidSpace

open Perfectoid

section OverAnalytic

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {A B C : Type*}
  [CommRing A] [UniformSpace A] [IsUniformAddGroup A] [IsTopologicalRing A] [IsTateRing A]
  [CompleteSpace A] [T2Space A]
  [CommRing B] [UniformSpace B] [IsUniformAddGroup B] [IsTopologicalRing B] [IsTateRing B]
  [CompleteSpace B] [T2Space B] [IsPerfectoidTateRing p B]
  [CommRing C] [UniformSpace C] [IsUniformAddGroup C] [IsTopologicalRing C] [IsTateRing C]
  [CompleteSpace C] [T2Space C] [IsPerfectoidTateRing p C]
  [Algebra A B] [Algebra A C] [IsAdicHom (algebraMap A B)] [IsAdicHom (algebraMap A C)]
  (S : Pair A) (T : Pair B) (U : Pair C) (hT : ∀ a ∈ S.plus, algebraMap A B a ∈ T.plus)
  (hU : ∀ a ∈ S.plus, algebraMap A C a ∈ U.plus)

/-- P2/fibre-products-over-analytic-base, pair-level core of `pullbackOverAnalyticSpaIso`: over a
complete Tate ring `A`, the uniform completed tensor product `B ⊗̂ᵘ_A C` with `inlᵘ`, `inrᵘ` is a
pushout of `(B, B⁺) ← (A, A⁺) → (C, C⁺)` among complete perfectoid Tate pairs (KL II Corollary
3.3.21 with the universal property of the uniformisation, KL I Definition 2.8.13); through Wedhorn
Proposition 8.25 this is the universal property of `Spa(B ⊗̂ᵘ_A C)` for perfectoid test spaces. -/
theorem pullbackOverAnalyticSpaIso_affinoid {E : Type*} [CommRing E] [UniformSpace E]
    [IsUniformAddGroup E] [IsTopologicalRing E] [IsTateRing E] [CompleteSpace E] [T2Space E]
    [IsPerfectoidTateRing p E] (V : Pair E) (φ : Pair.Hom T V) (ψ : Pair.Hom U V)
    (h : φ.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap A B) = ψ.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap A C)) :
    ∃! χ : Pair.Hom (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor S T U hT hU) V,
      χ.comp (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor.inl S T U hT hU) = φ ∧
        χ.comp (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor.inr S T U hT hU) = ψ := sorry

omit [Fact p.Prime] [IsPerfectoidTateRing p B] [IsPerfectoidTateRing p C] in
/-- P2/fibre-products-over-analytic-base, affinoid core of `pullbackOverAnalytic.surjective_points`:
every pair of points of `Spa(B, B⁺)` and `Spa(C, C⁺)` over the same point of `Spa(A, A⁺)` comes
from a point of `Spa(B ⊗̂ᵘ_A C)`: `Spa` of the uniformisation is homeomorphic to `Spa` of the
completed tensor product (AdicSpacesPartII:R0/uniformization (d)), and valuations amalgamate
(AdicSpacesPartII:R0/valuation-amalgamation). -/
theorem pullbackOverAnalytic.surjective_points_affinoid (y : spa T.plus) (z : spa U.plus)
    (h : Pair.Hom.spaComap (⟨algebraMap A B, IsAdicHom.continuous _, hT⟩ : Pair.Hom S T) y =
      Pair.Hom.spaComap (⟨algebraMap A C, IsAdicHom.continuous _, hU⟩ : Pair.Hom S U) z) :
    ∃ w : spa (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor S T U hT hU).plus,
      (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor.inl S T U hT hU).spaComap w = y ∧
        (Pair.uniformCompletedTensor.inr S T U hT hU).spaComap w = z := sorry

end OverAnalytic

end PerfectoidSpace

-- pullbackOverAnalytic_Cp_Qp: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.pullbackOverAnalytic`
