--   `|Y| ×_{|S|} |Z|`. [computation test]

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P2/products-in-perf (construction) -/

/-! For `X, Y ∈ Perf` the product `X × Y` exists in `Perf` (Berkeley Lemma 8.3.5; ECD proof of
Proposition 11.4); it is `X ×_{Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p)} Y` in adic spaces, over a base that is not perfectoid,
and `Perf` has no final object (Berkeley Remark 8.3.6). The affinoid charts are the pairs
`(C_{m,n}, C⁺_{m,n})`, stated through their universal property as
`PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart_ring`; the plus ring must contain `u_m`, `v_n`. -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prod: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). The product `X × Y` in `Perf`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodFst: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). The projection `X × Y → X`; likewise `prodSnd`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodLift: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). The unique `T → X × Y` for `T ∈ Perf`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.hasBinaryProducts: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). `HasBinaryProducts Perf`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart: not stated here as data; the pair `(C_{m,n}, C⁺_{m,n})` needs
--   the topology on `A ⊗_{𝔽_p} B` making `(A° ⊗ B°)[u_m, v_n]` open and `(ϖ ⊗ 1)`-adic, which
--   no library has (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 1). Its universal property is stated as
--   `PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart_ring`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart_hom_iff: not stated here as such; stated through the existence
--   form `PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart_ring` (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 1 for the chart).
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodChart_isRationalSubset: not stated here; needs `Spa` in `AdicSpace`
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). `Spa(C_{m,n}) ⊆ Spa(C_{m',n'})` is the rational subset
--   `{|u_m| ≤ 1, |v_n| ≤ 1}` for `m ≤ m'`, `n ≤ n'`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prod_eq_iUnion_prodChart: not stated here; needs gluing of adic spaces
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5). `X × Y = ⋃_{m,n} Spa(C_{m,n}, C⁺_{m,n})`, increasing.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prod_isPullback_spaFp: not stated here; needs `IsPullback` in `AdicSpace`
--   and `Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p)` (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5,
--   AdicSpacesPartII:R0/discrete-huber-pair-sheafy). `X × Y` is a pullback of
--   `X → Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p) ← Y` in adic spaces.
-- PerfectoidSpace.Perf.prodPerfectoidFieldsIso: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf`
--   (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). `Spa 𝔽_p((t^{1/p^∞})) × Spa 𝔽_p((s^{1/p^∞}))`
--   is the perfectoid punctured open unit disc over `𝔽_p((t^{1/p^∞}))`.

namespace PerfectoidSpace

open Perfectoid

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

/-- P2/products-in-perf, pair-level core of `Perf.prodChart` and `Perf.prodChart_hom_iff`: for
complete perfect Tate rings `A`, `B` of characteristic `p` with pairs `(A, A⁺)`, `(B, B⁺)`,
pseudo-uniformizers `ϖ ∈ A`, `ϖ' ∈ B` and `m, n ≥ 1`, there is a complete perfectoid Tate pair
`(C_{m,n}, C⁺_{m,n})` with morphisms from `(A, A⁺)` and `(B, B⁺)` such that morphisms from it to a
complete Huber pair `(R, R⁺)` with `R` Tate are the pairs `(φ, ψ)` with `φ(ϖ)^m ψ(ϖ')⁻¹ ∈ R⁺` and
`ψ(ϖ')^n φ(ϖ)⁻¹ ∈ R⁺` (Berkeley proof of Lemma 8.3.5; ECD proof of Proposition 11.4). -/
theorem Perf.prodChart_ring {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [UniformSpace A] [IsUniformAddGroup A]
    [IsTopologicalRing A] [IsTateRing A] [CompleteSpace A] [T2Space A] [CharP A p] [PerfectRing A p]
    [CommRing B] [UniformSpace B] [IsUniformAddGroup B] [IsTopologicalRing B] [IsTateRing B]
    [CompleteSpace B] [T2Space B] [CharP B p] [PerfectRing B p] (SA : Pair A) (SB : Pair B)
    (ϖ : A) (ϖ' : B) (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer ϖ) (hϖ' : IsPseudoUniformizer ϖ') (m n : ℕ)
    (hm : 1 ≤ m) (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    ∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : UniformSpace C) (_ : IsUniformAddGroup C)
      (_ : IsTopologicalRing C) (_ : IsTateRing C) (_ : CompleteSpace C) (_ : T2Space C)
      (_ : IsPerfectoidTateRing p C) (SC : Pair C) (φ₀ : Pair.Hom SA SC) (ψ₀ : Pair.Hom SB SC),
      ∀ (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [UniformSpace R] [IsUniformAddGroup R] [IsTopologicalRing R]
        [IsTateRing R] [CompleteSpace R] [T2Space R] (SR : Pair R) (φ : Pair.Hom SA SR)
        (ψ : Pair.Hom SB SR),
        (∃! χ : Pair.Hom SC SR, χ.comp φ₀ = φ ∧ χ.comp ψ₀ = ψ) ↔
          (∃ a ∈ SR.plus, φ.toRingHom ϖ ^ m = a * ψ.toRingHom ϖ') ∧
            ∃ b ∈ SR.plus, ψ.toRingHom ϖ' ^ n = b * φ.toRingHom ϖ := sorry

end PerfectoidSpace

-- prod_perfectoidFields: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). `Spa 𝔽_p((t^{1/p^∞})) × Spa 𝔽_p((s^{1/p^∞}))` is
--   `{0 < |s| < 1} ⊆ Spa 𝔽_p((t^{1/p^∞}))⟨s^{1/p^∞}⟩`, the union of the annuli
--   `{|t|^m ≤ |s| ≤ |t|^{1/n}}`; it is neither a point nor quasi-compact. [computation test]
-- prod_empty: not stated here; needs the empty adic space (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5).
--   `X × ∅ = ∅` for every `X ∈ Perf`. [degenerate test]
-- not_isPerfectoidSpace_spa_Fp_final: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.Perf` and the
--   discrete adic space `Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p)` (supplier: AdicSpacesPartII:R0/discrete-huber-pair-sheafy).
--   `Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p)` is not in `Perf`, `Perf` has no final object (Berkeley Remark 8.3.6), and
--   `X × Y` is not `X ×_Z Y` for a `Z ∈ Perf` in general. [non-example test]
-- prodChart_plus_open: not stated here; needs the topology on `A ⊗_{𝔽_p} B` of the chart
--   (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 1). For `A = B = 𝔽_p((t^{1/p^∞}))`, the integral closure of
--   `A⁺ ⊗ B⁺` is not open in `E`, so the plus ring must contain `u_m`, `v_n`. [non-example test]
-- prod_isPullback_spaFp: not stated here; needs `IsPullback` in `AdicSpace` (supplier: AdicSpaces
--   Layer 5). `X × Y` is a pullback of `X → Spa(𝔽_p, 𝔽_p) ← Y` in adic spaces and agrees with
--   Berkeley Lemma 8.3.5. [compatibility test]
-- prod_reduction_to_fields: not stated here; needs `PerfectoidSpace.pullback` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/fibre-products-of-perfectoid-spaces). Locally
--   `X × Y ≅ X ×_{Spa K_t} (Spa K_t × Spa K_s) ×_{Spa K_s} Y` (ECD proof of Proposition 11.4).
--   [characterisation test]

