/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P3/etale-is-strongly-etale (lemma) -/

-- The statements of this node are the packet items
-- `PerfectoidSpace.IsFiniteEtale.isStronglyFiniteEtale`, `PerfectoidSpace.IsEtale.isStronglyEtale`,
-- `PerfectoidSpace.IsStronglyFiniteEtale.iff_isFiniteEtale` and
-- `PerfectoidSpace.IsStronglyEtale.iff_isEtale`, recorded above as not stated (they need
-- perfectoid spaces over the anchor's adic spaces, PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). In
-- characteristic `p` they are P3/finite-etale-covers-in-characteristic-p, in general almost purity;
-- affinoid core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsStronglyFiniteEtale.iff_isFiniteEtale_affinoid`.

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P3/perfectoid-vs-analytic-finite-etale (comparison) -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.isPerfectoid_of_isFiniteEtale: not stated here; needs adic spaces finite étale
--   over a perfectoid space and the perfectoid predicate on adic spaces (supplier:
--   AdicEtaleGeometry:A1/finite-etale-morphism; PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space).
-- PerfectoidSpace.smallEtale_eq_adic: not stated here; needs AdicEtaleGeometry A1's sites of the
--   underlying adic space (supplier: AdicEtaleGeometry:A1/etale-site).

/-- P3/perfectoid-vs-analytic-finite-etale (c), algebraic core: for `S ∈ FÉt(R)` perfectoid for
its natural topology and `R⁺ ⊆ R°`, the integral closure of `R⁺` in `S` is a ring of integral
elements of `S`, so `(S, S⁺)` is a Huber pair and the plus ring of a finite étale morphism of
Huber pairs is forced (ECD after Definition 6.2; AdicEtaleGeometry:A1/finite-etale-affinoid-
algebra). -/
theorem isRingOfIntegralElements_integralClosure_affinoid (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {R S : Type u}
    [CommRing R] [UniformSpace R] [IsUniformAddGroup R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R]
    [CompleteSpace R] [T2Space R] [IsPerfectoidTateRing p R] [CommRing S] [_root_.Algebra R S]
    [Module.Finite R S] [_root_.Algebra.Etale R S] [UniformSpace S] [IsUniformAddGroup S]
    [IsModuleTopology R S] [IsTopologicalRing S] [IsTateRing S] (P : Pair R) :
    IsRingOfIntegralElements
      (integralClosure (P.plus.map (algebraMap R S)) S).toSubring := sorry

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P3/etale-morphisms-composition-base-change-open (lemma) -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.IsEtale.isStableUnderBaseChange: not stated here; needs fibre products of
--   perfectoid spaces and `MorphismProperty` on `PerfectoidSpace` (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/fibre-products-of-perfectoid-spaces). The statements (Berkeley
--   Proposition 7.5.2): (finite) étale morphisms are stable under composition, base change and
--   cancellation, are tilting invariant, and étale ones are open. Affinoid cores:
