is an uncountable strong limit of cofinality `> μ` (clause (iii) of the cutoff lemma,
DiamondsAndVStacks:D0/cutoff-cardinal), `#Mor(I) ≤ μ` and every `R_i` has `#R_i < κ'`, then the
limit is κ'-small: the bound does not grow with the diagram (ECD proof of Proposition 6.4). -/
theorem IsKappaSmall.completedFilteredColimit_of_lt_cof_affinoid {κ' μ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (hκ' : κ'.IsStrongLimit) (hκ'₀ : ℵ₀ < κ') (hcof : μ < κ'.ord.cof)
    (hJ : #(Σ i j : J, i ⟶ j) ≤ μ) (hF : ∀ j, #(F.obj j) < κ')
    (P : Pair (completedFilteredColimit p F j₀ ϖ)) : IsKappaSmall_affinoid κ' P := sorry

end CofilteredLimits

