/-! # Stage P7. Perfectoid tilde-limits, preperfectoid spaces and Frobenius-controlled towers

Names live in `TauCeti.Perfectoid` (ring level: Frobenius-controlled integral towers) and
`TauCeti.PerfectoidSpace` (tilde-limits, preperfectoid spaces, cofinality of levels).

* **Tilde-limits.** A perfectoid tilde-limit `X ~ lim X_i` (Scholze–Weinstein Definition 2.4.1),
  its residue-field variant `X ~′ lim X_i` (Sch12 Definition 7.14), good affinoid perfectoids,
  preperfectoid spaces and strong completions of spaces, the gluing and base-change theorems and
  the étale-topos comparison (Sch12 Theorem 7.17) all live on the anchor's category of adic
  spaces (AdicSpaces Layer 5) and on perfectoid spaces (PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space);
  Huber's tilde-limit is the carrier of ClassicalAdicEtaleCohomology H0. They are not-stated
  comments naming their supplier. Where the statement has a content about Huber pairs, it is
  stated for affinoid `X = Spa(R, R⁺)` and `X_i = Spa(A_i, A_i⁺)` under the suffix `_affinoid`:
  `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit_affinoid` (the homeomorphism onto the limit of the adic spectra
  and the density of `⋃ᵢ im(A_i)` in `R`), the completed direct limit of a filtered system of
  Tate pairs (`PerfectoidSpace.IsCompletedColimit_P7`, Scholze–Weinstein Proposition
  2.4.2), uniqueness of affinoid tilde-limits (Proposition 2.4.5), and the strong completion
  `PerfectoidSpace.strongCompletionPair` of a Tate pair (Definition 2.3.4). The systems are
  indexed by a filtered category on the ring side, i.e. by the opposite of the cofiltered index
  category of the spaces.
* **Frobenius-controlled integral towers** (`Perfectoid.FrobeniusTower`, Scholze's torsion
  paper, proof of Corollary III.2.19): `ϖ`-torsion-free `ϖ`-adically complete rings `A_m⁺` with
  eventual Frobenius lifts `w_m : A_{m+1}⁺/ϖ ≅ A_m⁺/ϖ^p`, their completed colimit
  `FrobeniusTower.completed`, the uniformity bound and the perfectoid Frobenius criterion.
* **Cofinality of levels** (`PerfectoidSpace.LevelFamily`, `PerfectoidSpace.CofinalityWitness`)
  for families of compact open subgroups, with Mathlib's `Functor.Initial`.

Sources: SW = Scholze–Weinstein, *Moduli of p-divisible groups*; Sch12 = Scholze, *Perfectoid
spaces*; Survey = Scholze, *Perfectoid spaces: a survey*; Torsion = Scholze, *On torsion in the
cohomology of locally symmetric varieties*; ECD = Scholze, *Étale cohomology of diamonds*; CHJ =
Chojecki–Hansen–Johansson, *Overconvergent modular forms and perfectoid Shimura curves*; BHW =
Birkbeck–Heuer–Williams, *Overconvergent Hilbert modular forms via perfectoid modular varieties*;
BMS1 = Bhatt–Morrow–Scholze, *Integral p-adic Hodge theory*; KL = Kedlaya–Liu, *Relative p-adic
Hodge theory* I. -/

noncomputable section

namespace TauCeti

universe u

open _root_.Topology _root_.Filter _root_.CategoryTheory _root_.CategoryTheory.Limits
open Huber ValuationSpectrum

/-! ## PerfectoidSpaces:P7/perfectoid-tilde-limit (definition) -/

-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit: not stated here; needs the anchor's analytic adic spaces with
--   quasicompact quasiseparated morphisms, perfectoid spaces and the limit `lim |X_i|` of their
--   underlying spaces (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 5, PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space; Huber's
--   carrier ClassicalAdicEtaleCohomology:H0/tilde-limits-and-cohomological-continuity). Affinoid
--   core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.homeomorph: not stated here; needs `IsTildeLimit` (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). Affinoid core: the fields `IsTildeLimit_affinoid.isEmbedding` and
--   `IsTildeLimit_affinoid.range_eq`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.dense: not stated here; needs the structure sheaves `O_X`, `O_{X_i}`
--   on all opens (supplier: AdicSpaces Layer 3, Layer 5). Affinoid core (for the cover `U = X`):
--   the field `IsTildeLimit_affinoid.dense`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.toHuber: not stated here; needs Huber's tilde-limit predicate on
--   qcqs adic spaces (supplier: ClassicalAdicEtaleCohomology:H0/tilde-limits-and-cohomological-
--   continuity).
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.iff_goodCover: not stated here; needs good affinoid perfectoids,
--   i.e. affinoid perfectoid opens of a perfectoid space (supplier:
--   PerfectoidSpaces:P2/affinoid-perfectoid-space, AdicSpaces Layer 5).
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.lift: not stated here; needs morphisms of adic spaces (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5). Affinoid core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.lift_affinoid`
--   (PerfectoidSpaces:P7/tilde-limit-perfectoid-uniqueness).
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.uniqueIso: not stated here; needs isomorphisms of perfectoid spaces
--   (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). Affinoid core:
--   `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.uniqueIso_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.ofIso: not stated here; needs isomorphisms of perfectoid spaces
--   (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/perfectoid-space). Affinoid core:
--   `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.ofIso_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.restrict: not stated here; needs open subspaces of perfectoid
--   spaces and of the `X_i` (supplier: PerfectoidSpaces:P2/open-subspaces-of-perfectoid-spaces,
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5).
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.reindex: not stated here; needs `IsTildeLimit` (supplier: AdicSpaces
--   Layer 5). Affinoid core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.reindex_affinoid`
--   (PerfectoidSpaces:P7/tilde-limit-cofinal-change).
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.const: not stated here; needs `IsTildeLimit` (supplier: AdicSpaces
--   Layer 5). Affinoid core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.const_affinoid`.
-- PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.spectralSpace: not stated here; needs `IsTildeLimit` (supplier:
--   AdicSpaces Layer 5; DiamondsAndVStacks:D0/cofiltered-limits-of-spectral-spaces). Affinoid
--   core: `PerfectoidSpace.IsTildeLimit.spectralSpace_affinoid`.

namespace PerfectoidSpace

section TildeLimitAffinoid

variable {J : Type*} [Category J] {A : J → Type*} [∀ j, CommRing (A j)]
  [∀ j, TopologicalSpace (A j)] [∀ j, IsTopologicalRing (A j)] [∀ j, IsHuberRing (A j)]
  (P : ∀ j, Pair (A j)) (f : ∀ {i j : J}, (i ⟶ j) → Pair.Hom (P i) (P j))
  {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsHuberRing R]
  (Q : Pair R) (g : ∀ j, Pair.Hom (P j) Q)

/-- P7/perfectoid-tilde-limit (structure, affinoid core of `IsTildeLimit`): for a filtered
system of Huber pairs `(A_j, A_j⁺)` (the coordinate rings of a cofiltered system of affinoids
`X_j = Spa(A_j, A_j⁺)`) and a compatible cone `g_j : (A_j, A_j⁺) → (R, R⁺)`, the two clauses of
Scholze–Weinstein Definition 2.4.1 for `X = Spa(R, R⁺)` and the cover `U = X`: (a) the map
`|X| → lim_j |X_j|`, `x ↦ (g_j^* x)_j`, is a homeomorphism, i.e. an embedding into `∏_j |X_j|`
with image the compatible families; (b) `⋃_j im(A_j → R)` is dense in `R`. -/
structure IsTildeLimit_affinoid [IsFiltered J] : Prop where
  /-- The cone is compatible: `g_j ∘ f_a = g_i` for `a : i ⟶ j`. -/
  comm : ∀ {i j : J} (a : i ⟶ j), (g j).toRingHom.comp (f a).toRingHom = (g i).toRingHom
  /-- (a) `|X| → ∏_j |X_j|` is an embedding. -/
  isEmbedding : IsEmbedding fun (x : spa Q.plus) (j : J) ↦ (g j).spaComap x
  /-- (a) its image is `lim_j |X_j|`, the compatible families. -/
  range_eq : Set.range (fun (x : spa Q.plus) (j : J) ↦ (g j).spaComap x) =
    {y | ∀ (i j : J) (a : i ⟶ j), (f a).spaComap (y j) = y i}
  /-- (b) the union of the images of the `A_j` is dense in `R`. -/
  dense : Dense (⋃ j, Set.range (g j).toRingHom)

/-- P7/perfectoid-tilde-limit (other, affinoid core of `IsTildeLimit.spectralSpace`): if the
`Spa(A_j, A_j⁺)` are spectral, so is `Spa(R, R⁺)`, and the projections are spectral maps
(Sch12 Remark 7.15; Stacks Tag 0A2Z; DiamondsAndVStacks:D0/cofiltered-limits-of-spectral-spaces). -/
theorem IsTildeLimit.spectralSpace_affinoid [IsFiltered J] (h : IsTildeLimit_affinoid P f Q g)
    [∀ j, SpectralSpace (spa (P j).plus)] :
    SpectralSpace (spa Q.plus) ∧ ∀ j, IsSpectralMap (g j).spaComap := sorry

/-- P7/perfectoid-tilde-limit (functoriality, affinoid core of `IsTildeLimit.ofIso`): an affinoid
tilde-limit transports along an isomorphism of Huber pairs `(R, R⁺) ≅ (R', R'⁺)`. -/
theorem IsTildeLimit.ofIso_affinoid [IsFiltered J] (h : IsTildeLimit_affinoid P f Q g)
    {R' : Type*} [CommRing R'] [TopologicalSpace R'] [IsTopologicalRing R'] [IsHuberRing R']
    {Q' : Pair R'} (e : Pair.Hom Q Q') (e' : Pair.Hom Q' Q)
    (he : (e'.comp e).toRingHom = RingHom.id R) (he' : (e.comp e').toRingHom = RingHom.id R') :
    IsTildeLimit_affinoid P f Q' fun j ↦ e.comp (g j) := sorry

/-- P7/tilde-limit-from-completed-colimit (structure, affinoid): `(R, R⁺)` with the cone `g_j` is
the *completed direct limit* of the filtered system `(A_j, A_j⁺)` in the Tate case of
Scholze–Weinstein Proposition 2.4.2: the rings of definition `A_{j,0}` are mapped into one
another, `ϖ ∈ R` is a pseudouniformiser coming from some `A_{j,0}`, the closure `R₀` of the subring
generated by the `g_j(A_{j,0})` is an open ring of definition of `R` with the `ϖ`-adic topology
(`R₀` is the `ϖ`-adic completion of `colim_j A_{j,0}`), `⋃_j g_j(A_j)` is dense in `R`, and `R⁺`
is the closure of the integral closure of the subring generated by the `g_j(A_j⁺)`. Also used by
PerfectoidSpaces:P7/frobenius-tower-completion (`FrobeniusTower.isCompletedDirectLimit`). -/
structure IsCompletedColimit_P7 [IsFiltered J] (A₀ : ∀ j, Subring (A j)) (ϖ : R) :
    Prop where
  /-- The cone is compatible. -/
  comm : ∀ {i j : J} (a : i ⟶ j), (g j).toRingHom.comp (f a).toRingHom = (g i).toRingHom
  /-- The rings of definition are mapped into one another. -/
  map_le : ∀ {i j : J} (a : i ⟶ j), (A₀ i).map (f a).toRingHom ≤ A₀ j
  /-- `ϖ` is a pseudouniformiser of `R`. -/
  isPseudoUniformizer : IsPseudoUniformizer ϖ
  /-- `ϖ` comes from a ring of definition at a finite level. -/
  exists_mem : ∃ j, ∃ x ∈ A₀ j, (g j).toRingHom x = ϖ
  /-- `R₀ = closure of ⟨⋃_j g_j(A_{j,0})⟩` is an open ring of definition with ideal `(ϖ)`. -/
  exists_pairOfDefinition : ∃ (D : PairOfDefinition R) (h : ϖ ∈ D.ringOfDefinition),
    D.ringOfDefinition = (Subring.closure (⋃ j, (g j).toRingHom '' (A₀ j))).topologicalClosure ∧
      D.idealOfDefinition = Ideal.span {⟨ϖ, h⟩}
  /-- `⋃_j g_j(A_j)` is dense in `R`. -/
  dense : Dense (⋃ j, Set.range (g j).toRingHom)
  /-- `R⁺` is the closure of the integral closure of `⟨⋃_j g_j(A_j⁺)⟩`. -/
  plus_eq : Q.plus = (integralClosure (Subring.closure (⋃ j, (g j).toRingHom '' (P j).plus))
    R).toSubring.topologicalClosure

end TildeLimitAffinoid

/-- P7/perfectoid-tilde-limit (example, affinoid core of `IsTildeLimit.const`): the one-object
system on a Huber pair, with the identity cone, is an affinoid tilde-limit. -/
theorem IsTildeLimit.const_affinoid {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [TopologicalSpace R]
    [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsHuberRing R] (Q : Pair R) :
    IsTildeLimit_affinoid (J := Discrete PUnit) (fun _ ↦ Q) (fun _ ↦ Pair.Hom.id Q) Q
      fun _ ↦ Pair.Hom.id Q := sorry

